  "story": "High in the Kumaon hills, where India meets Nepal, mornings still begin with woodsmoke, cowbells and the smell of wet pine.\n\nKumaoni Roots started from a simple worry: the food that reaches our cities has travelled far from where it was grown, and somewhere along the way it lost its honesty. We wanted to bring back the taste we grew up with, made the way our grandparents made it.\n\nEverything we sell is made in the villages along the India–Nepal border, far from the factories and fumes of the plains. There are no chemicals, no shortcuts and no adulteration, only clean mountain air, patient hands and traditional methods.\n\nBehind every jar and packet are small local farmers and women of the village, and we make sure they are paid fairly for their work. When you buy from us, you take home a piece of the mountains and help a family stay on the land they love.\n\nWe begin with ghee, turmeric, spices and pulses, but this is only the start. More treasures of the hills will follow.",
